Issue: Parent N5 (52669ee, average 0.5122) gave the harness a second derivation of the answer, and its own traces price the two halves of that pass apart. The rewriting half paid: 4 of its 5 LawBench gains are the draft's own answer re-written in the key's characters -- `生产、销售伪劣产品罪` -> the listed `生产、销售伪劣产品` at [[LawBench/conversations/0012/sample-0.json]], `拐卖妇女` -> the listed `拐卖妇女、儿童` at [[LawBench/conversations/0036/sample-1.json]] -- and part of its USPTO gains. The re-deciding half cost: 14 of the 19 Symptom2Disease rewrites overrode a correct draft (bronchial asthma -> pneumonia in 6 samples, malaria -> dengue in 3) and the 2 LawBench losses demoted a listed specific string to a shorter listed one (`销售假冒注册商标的商品` -> `假冒注册商标`). The pass's own text shows it never audited anything: it re-read the case, reached the same single charge and rationalised the draft it had been shown -- at [[LawBench/conversations/0035/sample-0.json]] it writes three sentences about the assault and returns `故意伤害` against a gold that also carries the prostitution charges, and at [[LawBench/conversations/0044/sample-0.json]] it writes `对照答案键：案情特征与列表中的'强制猥亵、侮辱妇女'完全吻合`, i.e. it looks up the draft in the key and confirms it. So on the 12 LawBench samples whose gold carries charges the draft left out it changed nothing, while the family it could have fixed is the one it was re-deciding past. An offline pass over the parent's own 260 samples (no model calls) measures the licence's room: on the parent's 48 wrong LawBench samples, 11 are answers that name the entry the case calls for in characters the memory never writes (`窝藏` for the listed `窝藏、包庇`, `盗窃罪` for the listed `盗窃`, `非法获取公民个人信息罪` for the listed `非法获取公民个人信息`, `帮助毁灭证据` for the listed `帮助毁灭、伪造证据`, `伪造金融票证` for the listed `伪造、变造金融票证`), while Symptom2Disease has 100/100 answers whose entries are already listed strings and USPTO 60/60 answers that are combinations the memory never wrote, so a check licensed to rewrite an answer's entries into the memory's own spelling is a structural no-op on both of those tasks and only bites on the task whose answer is a set of joined entries. The same offline pass says the other licence is a trap: 20 of those 48 wrong samples (10 questions) are set-omission cases whose missing charges have no support in the facts at all -- question 2's facts mention no weapon and no brawl, question 35's no prostitution, question 48's no 妨害公务 -- so a pass licensed to add entries would be guessing at labels the abridged case cannot carry.

Modification: the harness's second look at the answer is now a spelling check instead of a second derivation. `solver/passes.py` replaces `rederive` with `conform`: one model call, the same model, that gets the case, the memory's answer key and the answer the conversation produced, and is told that nothing here decides the answer again -- which entries the answer is made of is settled -- and that it must take the answer's entries one at a time, in the answer's own order, find the listed string that is the same entry and copy that string exactly (so a name, title or category word the answer added and the list never uses, a piece of a joined name it dropped, or punctuation the list does not write, is corrected), leave an entry the list does not write as the answer wrote it apart from the shape of the string itself, and keep every entry the answer has -- never adding one it did not choose and never writing a different entry in place of one it chose. `solver/agent.py` wraps the compiled agent in `ConformedAgent`, the same wrapper structure N5 used: the conversation is left as it is (it stays the trace of what was retrieved and argued), the pass's text replaces the last message when it carries an answer, and a pass that fails, is filtered or returns nothing leaves the draft standing, so the pass cannot cost a sample by erroring. `conform` additionally rejects a pass output that carries no `"final_answer"` field, so a pass that answers in prose cannot replace an answer either. Retrieval, the answer key, the memory and `prepare_memory.py` are untouched; no dataset name, label list, keyword list or dataset-identity branch was added and no Val/Test label is fed back.

